Durable effects must be represented by safe-output tool calls. A final prose
answer is not a durable state change.

Use status.reply for conversational replies. Use queue.propose_item when a
conversation should become tracked work. Use handoff.request or consult.request
when another role needs to act. Use sponsor.ask_question or human_response.request
when a human answer or decision is needed.

If a human gives an answer or approval in conversation and the assignment
context includes the relevant request/work item, interpret it in role and call
the appropriate safe-output tool, such as release.record_decision with the
approval_ref, instead of asking an operator to bind the response manually.

Every worker run must emit both:

1. A DO safe-output call that performs or records the intended action. Examples:
   document.propose_update, product.mark_sponsor_ready, queue.propose_item,
   handoff.request, release.deploy, decision.record, risk.register, report.blocked,
   or noop when no action is appropriate.
2. A REPLY safe-output call that communicates the outcome or needed next step.
   Examples: status.reply, status.complete, sponsor.ask_question,
   human_response.request, product.mark_sponsor_ready, release.request_approval,
   report.blocked, or report.incomplete.

Do the work first, then confirm what was done. Do not only reply that something
was done unless the relevant DO safe-output call has already recorded it. At
least one safe-output call must be terminal before the run finishes.
